From ca18bfd33b74f550ab9b125b035fa14decf7efd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:10:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] Fix what ESLint found; targeted disables with reasons
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hand fixes (behaviour kept unless noted): TanStack Form's deprecated useStore → useSelector,
the starter's ensureQueryData → query({ staleTime: 'static' }), React 19 use()/<Context value> in
our own code, conditional rendering that could print "0" (a kanban card with no labels and a
stepper description did), real out-of-range reads made explicit, unsafe `any` flows typed,
non-breaking spaces escaped, `??` only where it's equivalent.

Kept on purpose, each disabled on its line with the reason: shadcn/Radix patterns (context in
ui/, calendar slots, chart CSS variables, aria-invalid on picker triggers, combobox triggers
whose aria-controls comes from PopoverTrigger), React Compiler rules on working effects (reading
storage after mount, syncing drafts from props, Embla, TanStack Table/Virtual), keyboard-reachable
scroll regions, index keys on append-only or static lists.

Config: starter routes may export Route next to components and throw redirect()/notFound().
AGENTS.md and the README describe the new tooling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Te9bARZBkSfcxCSZLhK4ZW
